{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor actively used the clinical workspace, corrected a dangerous family-directed concealment plan, reconciled peri‑operative medications, and taught red flags. However, the initial turn (lite_evt_00031) gave a generic 1‑week re‑examination plan without confirming the actual urgent next‑day anaesthesia visit, treated the follow‑up CT as a default, and omitted verifying what the patient already knew, making the discharge‑transition plan actionable but with a minor responsibility‑chain gap. No serious error was committed, so the maximum allowed grade is 2 (borderline).",
